C={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-thirtyfifth-d3-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]};P={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]}
N={
"mcallister25_interspeech":("Voice training is an interactional skill, so a useful tool must show a learner what changed while they speak and remain usable in practice.","Resonance is felt and heard, but a display can overwhelm a learner or turn a gradual skill into a misleading single score.","Show raw spectra or prescribe a fixed target value and assume users can interpret it.","Build a browser tool that gives real-time vocal-resonance biofeedback and evaluate whether intended users can complete tasks and understand the feedback.","The study combines real-time acoustic analysis, visual feedback, and a usability evaluation for gender-affirming voice training.","The design treats feedback as part of a human learning loop: measurement matters only if a person can notice it, interpret it, and act on it.","The paper reports a working web application and usability findings supporting its use as a training aid.","Small usability sample, task design, browser/audio conditions, and self-report limit claims about long-term learning or clinical outcomes."),
"do25b_interspeech":("A speech system should identify toxic spans in Vietnamese audio without hiding which words triggered the judgment.","Toxicity depends on language, context, and span boundaries; speech recognition errors can change both the words and the location of the alleged harm.","Classify the whole utterance or run a text toxicity model on an imperfect transcript and treat its spans as exact.","Create an audio-based Vietnamese toxic-span task that preserves local evidence and evaluates both detection and boundary selection.","ViToSA builds an audio dataset and task for locating toxic spans in Vietnamese speech utterances.","The prediction target is localized: the system must connect acoustic input to a particular interval or word span rather than only assign a sentence label.","The paper reports benchmark results for Vietnamese audio toxic-span detection.","Dataset construction, annotation agreement, language, ASR errors, and social context bound the result; a benchmark score is not a complete safety policy."),
"dong25e_interspeech":("Respiratory sounds are noisy measurements of a changing physical process, and a classifier needs to preserve disease-relevant events while suppressing irrelevant noise.","Breath sounds overlap in time and vary by microphone, patient, environment, and pathology; fixed denoising can remove the very irregularity being measured.","Apply one fixed noise filter or classify raw recordings without testing how denoising changes the signal.","Use an adaptive differential denoising procedure whose behavior changes with the observed respiratory signal, then test classification.","The paper proposes adaptive differential denoising for respiratory-sound classification and compares it with less adaptive processing.","Denoising is part of the measurement model: the classifier can only learn a clinical distinction if the preprocessing preserves the relevant temporal-acoustic structure.","The paper reports improved respiratory-sound classification with the proposed denoising approach.","Dataset, labels, recording hardware, noise conditions, and evaluation split limit generalization to clinical deployment or diagnosis."),
"hsiao25_interspeech":("A spoken-language model trained end to end may learn new tasks while forgetting how to perform tasks it already knew.","Speech, text, vocabulary, and task behavior are updated together; reducing forgetting can also reduce learning of the new objective or distort the shared representation.","Train only on the new data, freeze everything, or assume a larger model automatically retains old abilities.","Compare mitigation strategies for catastrophic forgetting during end-to-end spoken-language-model training, including how data and parameter updates are controlled.","The study evaluates forgetting-mitigation strategies for end-to-end training of spoken language models.","The core tradeoff is retention versus adaptation: an update is useful only if it improves the new task without erasing previously learned speech-language behavior.","The paper reports comparative forgetting and adaptation results across the tested strategies.","Tasks, training order, model size, data mixture, and retention metrics bound the conclusions; results do not establish lifelong learning in open deployment."),
"cumani25_interspeech":("A speaker-recognition backend must decide whether recordings belong to the same person, while evaluation rankings can change with scoring, calibration, and trial composition.","A benchmark result is not only an embedding result: backend assumptions determine how scores are normalized and how errors are traded off.","Compare systems using one unexamined score or treat the best embedding as automatically the best verification system.","Analyze the ABC classification backends used for NIST SRE24 and separate representation quality from backend scoring behavior.","The paper studies backend choices for speaker classification/verification in the NIST SRE24 setting.","Verification is a decision pipeline: embeddings, score computation, calibration, and operating point jointly produce the accepted/rejected decision.","The paper reports how the analyzed backends behave on the NIST SRE24 evaluation conditions.","Benchmark protocol, language/channel conditions, calibration, and chosen operating points limit claims beyond SRE24."),
"guo25_interspeech":("A speech codec should use few bits while preserving speech quality and should let a downstream system change speaker identity without accidentally carrying the original identity through the code.","Compression and identity are entangled: a code that preserves every detail spends bits, while a code that removes identity may damage linguistic content or naturalness.","Compress a standard speaker-dependent representation and assume the decoder will separate identity later.","Learn a low-bitrate discrete code that is decoupled from speaker identity, then condition decoding on the desired speaker.","LSCodec targets low-bitrate, speaker-decoupled discrete speech coding for controllable reconstruction or conversion.","The code is a bottleneck with a division of labor: linguistic/acoustic content crosses the bottleneck, while speaker identity is supplied separately at decoding.","The paper reports low-bitrate codec and speaker-decoupling results on its reconstruction/conversion evaluations.","Bitrate, speaker set, decoder, datasets, and disentanglement tests bound the claim; identity leakage can remain outside the tested conditions."),
"kwok25b_interspeech":("Contextual biasing should help a recognizer spell a user's rare keyword, but it should not turn every acoustically similar word into that keyword.","Synthetic training examples can be plentiful yet unrealistic; a fixed cost for all keywords ignores how often each keyword is confused and how context changes the error.","Add a uniform decoding bonus or generate random keyword examples without modeling which confusions matter.","Use a keyword-aware cost function when training synthetic contextual-biasing data so difficult and useful examples receive the right pressure.","The paper improves synthetic-data training for contextual biasing with a keyword-aware cost function.","The training objective changes the data's influence according to the keyword-level error structure; the goal is targeted correction rather than blanket bias.","The paper reports improved contextual-biasing performance for the proposed synthetic-data objective.","Keyword lists, synthetic-data quality, language, decoder, and evaluation distribution limit generalization; better keyword recall can still create false activations."),
"escobargrisales25_interspeech":("Parkinson's speech can show changes in both how sounds are produced and how language is organized, so one signal family may give an incomplete picture.","Acoustic and linguistic symptoms vary across speakers and tasks, and changes can be correlated without one causing the other.","Use only a speech-rate/acoustic score or only a transcript-based linguistic score as a complete disease marker.","Measure acoustic and linguistic production synchronously in the same speech material and examine their joint relationship.","The study synchronizes analysis of abnormal acoustic and linguistic production in Parkinson's speech.","Synchronous observation aligns two levels of behavior in time, allowing co-occurrence to be studied without pretending that either level alone explains the condition.","The paper reports coordinated acoustic and linguistic findings in Parkinson's speech.","Cohort, task, disease stage, annotation, and statistical design limit clinical generalization; association is not diagnosis or causation."),
}
